  "enunciado": "A harbor master is labeling fifteen dock zones. Color each region with red, green or blue. A region pair separated by a dash denotes a direct link. Linked regions must have different colors. The links work both ways. The regions are Basin, Bay, Crane, Depot, Float, Inlet, Jetty, Lock, Mole, Pier, Quay, Ramp, Reef, Slip, Yard.\n1. Pier is red.\n2. Jetty is blue.\n3. Pier–Yard.\n4. Jetty–Pier, Jetty–Ramp.\n5. Bay–Inlet, Bay–Jetty, Bay–Pier, Bay–Quay, Bay–Ramp.\n6. Ramp–Slip.\n7. Basin–Depot, Basin–Jetty, Basin–Lock, Basin–Pier, Basin–Reef.\n8. Lock–Mole, Lock–Ramp, Lock–Yard.\n9. Quay–Ramp.\n10. Depot–Inlet, Depot–Quay, Depot–Slip.\n11. Crane–Depot, Crane–Float, Crane–Lock, Crane–Pier.\n12. Float–Inlet, Float–Jetty, Float–Lock.\n13. Slip–Yard.\n14. Reef–Slip.\n15. Mole–Pier, Mole–Slip.\nFor each named region, give its color.",
